\title{Code block ignore markers}
\tag{test}

\p{
  This tree exercises the new \code{forester-ignore: start/end} markers. The block below has two collapsed regions: one with a summary in parens, one without. Hover the code block to see the toolbar; click the expand icon to open the modal with the full source.
}

\codeblock{python}{
  \startverb
def build_index(rows):
    table = {}
    # forester-ignore: start (validation + normalization)
    if not isinstance(rows, list):
        raise TypeError("rows must be a list")
    rows = [r for r in rows if r is not None]
    for r in rows:
        if "id" not in r:
            raise ValueError(f"missing id: {r!r}")
    # forester-ignore: end

    for row in rows:
        table[row["id"]] = row

    # forester-ignore: start
    for k, v in list(table.items()):
        if v.get("deleted"):
            del table[k]
    # forester-ignore: end

    return table
    \stopverb
}

\p{
  A second block, this one without any markers, should show only a single copy button as before (toolbar with one icon).
}

\codeblock{python}{
  \startverb
def greet(name: str) -> str:
    return f"hello, {name}"
    \stopverb
}
